#
# Keeps the stock configstore HAL from being started at all.
#
# It cannot run under Android 15. The vendor sandboxes it with a seccomp filter
# written for Android 10, and the libraries it now links against call a syscall
# that filter does not allow:
#
#     libminijail[701]: blocked syscall: gettid
#     init: Service 'vendor.configstore-hal' (pid 701) received signal 31
#
# Signal 31 is SIGSYS. Left alone, init restarts it every five seconds for as
# long as the phone is on -- seventy-nine errors in the first six minutes. The
# filter lives in /vendor, which this device ships as a prebuilt image, so it
# cannot be widened.
#
# Nothing needs the HAL any more: device.mk sets the thirteen
# ro.surface_flinger.* properties that SurfaceFlinger, libEGL and
# WindowManagerService consult before asking it, so they never do. See the
# comment there.
#
# "stop" rather than anything else because init marks a stopped service
# disabled, and a later class_start skips it. The trigger is "on init" and not
# something later because the service is in class hal *and* animation, and the
# animation class starts early; init parses every .rc file before running any
# action, so the service is already known by then.
on init
    stop vendor.configstore-hal
